<title>USA: HemaCare Corp says Red Cross settles suit.</title>
<headline>HemaCare Corp says Red Cross settles suit.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>HemaCare Corp and the American Red Cross said on Wednesday that they have settled HemaCare's pending lawsuit.</p>
<p>Terms of the settlement are confidential.</p>
<p>HemaCare had sued the Red Cross in federal court in December 1995, alleging that the Red Cross' pricing practices in Los Angeles and Orange Counties for platelets and other blood products violated the antitrust laws and California unfair trade practice laws, it said.</p>
<p>The Red Cross denied that its pricing practices were unlawful.</p>
</text>
